codeword : 0110011
error at None: syndrome 0, data 1011
error at 5   : syndrome 5, data 1011

--- Follow-up: Double-bit flip (positions 3 and 5) ---
  Corrupted rx=0100111 -> syndrome 6, miscorrected data=0101 (WRONG; expected 1011!)

--- 16-bit Sensor Word Hamming Sizing ---
  m = 16 bits -> smallest r with 2^r >= m+r+1 is r = 5 (2^5=32 >= 22)
  Codeword = 21 bits | Overhead = 5/21 = 23.81%
  Min Hamming distance d_min = 3 -> detects 2 errors, corrects 1 error
  Received 0110111 -> syndrome 5 (bit 5 flipped), corrected data = 1011

--- Alternative Concept: BER = 1e-3 (Hamming FEC vs 40 ms ARQ) ---
  Hamming(21,16) FEC : 21 bits/reading | >=2-bit fail prob = 0.0207% | avg extra delay = 0.0083 ms
  ARQ (16b + parity) : 17.27 bits/reading | frame error prob = 1.59% | avg extra delay = 0.645 ms (tail = 40 ms)
  Verdict: FEC suits noisy real-time radio/video/5G links because it eliminates 40 ms retransmission stalls.
